<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch August producer prices rise 1.1 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Dutch August producer prices rise 1.1 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>VOORBURG, Netherlands 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dutch producer price index (PPI) for manufactured goods was provisionally unchanged in August from July, giving a 1.1 percent rise year-on-year, the Central Bureau of Statistics (CBS) said.  </p>
<p> DUTCH PRODUCER PRICES	  Aug 96    July 96     Aug 95</p>
<p> Index (base 1990)		101.9	101.9*     100.8</p>
<p> Month-on-month pct change     flat	 +0.2*	+0.6</p>
<p> Year-on-year pct change	 +1.1	 +1.7*	+2.5</p>
<p> Subindex domestic prices     106.0	105.9	104.1</p>
<p> Subindex export prices	  98.7	 98.7	 98.2</p>
<p>* The July data were upwardly revised by 0.1 percentage point.  </p>
<p>The CBS said that the stable producer prices resulted from higher prices for oil products, while prices of oil derivatives in the petrochemicals industry fell.</p>
<p>Prices also fell in the paper and base metal industry.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
